1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,899
The Titanic carried more
lifeboats than the law required.

2
00:00:03,949 --> 00:00:06,913
So why did about 1,500 people die?

3
00:00:06,963 --> 00:00:12,377
The iceberg sank the ship.
An old rule explains why so many died with it.

4
00:00:15,767 --> 00:00:18,646
British lifeboat rules
went by a ship's size,

5
00:00:18,696 --> 00:00:21,838
in a table last updated in 1894.

6
00:00:21,888 --> 00:00:25,819
Back then, the biggest
liner was about 13,000 tons.

7
00:00:25,869 --> 00:00:28,488
So the table stopped at 10,000 and up.

8
00:00:28,538 --> 00:00:34,793
The Titanic was 46,000. To the law,
it was the same as a ship a fifth its size.

9
00:00:34,843 --> 00:00:38,322
So the rules asked for 962 seats.

10
00:00:38,372 --> 00:00:41,323
The Titanic had 1,178.

11
00:00:41,373 --> 00:00:44,816
On board: more than 2,200 people.

12
00:00:45,033 --> 00:00:48,733
Why not update it?
Ships now had watertight compartments.

13
00:00:48,783 --> 00:00:50,836
And radio could call for help.

14
00:00:50,886 --> 00:00:54,313
Lifeboats weren't meant to hold
everyone. They were ferries,

15
00:00:54,363 --> 00:00:55,870
out to rescue ships.

16
00:00:55,920 --> 00:01:01,538
In 1909, it worked. The liner Republic,
struck in fog, radioed for help,

17
00:01:01,588 --> 00:01:05,076
and about 1,500 people
were ferried to safety.

18
00:01:05,667 --> 00:01:08,405
At 11:40 p.m. on April 14,

19
00:01:08,455 --> 00:01:10,711
the Titanic hit an iceberg.

20
00:01:10,761 --> 00:01:15,049
Five compartments flooded.
It was built to survive four.

21
00:01:15,099 --> 00:01:17,788
It had two hours and forty minutes.

22
00:01:18,167 --> 00:01:22,300
The nearest ship, the Californian,
was less than 20 miles away.

23
00:01:22,350 --> 00:01:25,267
Its only radio operator had gone to bed.

24
00:01:25,317 --> 00:01:28,848
The Carpathia heard the call,
58 miles away.

25
00:01:28,898 --> 00:01:32,196
It arrived more than an
hour and a half too late.

26
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:36,508
The ferry plan fell apart.
And the boats left half empty.

27
00:01:36,558 --> 00:01:39,312
The first one lowered could hold 65.

28
00:01:39,362 --> 00:01:41,094
It carried 28.

29
00:01:41,144 --> 00:01:47,473
About 710 people survived,
in boats with room for 1,178.

30
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:52,100
Within two years, nations signed
the first treaty on safety at sea:

31
00:01:52,150 --> 00:01:56,743
a lifeboat seat for everyone,
and radios staffed day and night.

32
00:01:56,793 --> 00:02:00,700
And an ice patrol that still
watches the North Atlantic today.

33
00:02:00,750 --> 00:02:03,048
The Titanic didn't break the rules.

34
00:02:03,098 --> 00:02:04,643
That was the problem.

